// TOFFCTL.QS0 - multi-qubit controlled gates and classical control.
//
// Demonstrates: TOFF (Toffoli), MCX (multi-controlled-X), CSWAP (Fredkin),
// and IF-driven gates.
//
// Qubit-level explanation:
//   X 0, X 1 set the controls of the three-qubit gates. Then:
//     TOFF 0 1 2    flips qubit 2 iff qubits 0 and 1 are both |1>. They are,
//                   so qubit 2 becomes |1>.
//     MCX 7 3       is an X on qubit 3 controlled by every bit set in the
//                   mask 7 = 0b111, i.e. qubits 0, 1 and 2. All three are
//                   now |1>, so qubit 3 flips to |1>.
//     X 4, X 5      set the Fredkin control and one of the swapped qubits.
//     CSWAP 4 5 6   swaps qubits 5 and 6 iff qubit 4 is |1>. Since it is,
//                   the |1> moves from qubit 5 to qubit 6.
//   Finally MEASURE 0 writes the deterministic outcome 1 into c0, and the
//   IF block flips qubit 1 back to |0>.
//
//   Every step is deterministic (no superpositions are created), so all 1000
//   shots report the single final state. The histogram is printed in the
//   |q6 q5 q4 q3 q2 q1 q0> ordering, giving |1011101> (q6=1, q5=0, q4=1,
//   q3=1, q2=1, q1=0, q0=1).
//
// Run:
//   plasma run examples/TOFFCTL.QS0 --shots 1000
QUBITS 7
X 0
X 1
TOFF 0 1 2
MCX 7 3
X 4
X 5
CSWAP 4 5 6
MEASURE 0 -> c0
IF c0 == 1 THEN
  X 1
ENDIF
SHOT 1000
PRINT
END